# invert

- Label: Invert
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 3 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/invert.html
- Summary (EN): Inverts the values of an incoming layer, VDB or attribute. By default it complements the values (1 - x), swapping black and white.
- Résumé (FR) : Inverse les valeurs d'une couche par complément, négation ou inverse, sur les canaux choisis, avec masque optionnel.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer, VDB or attribute to invert", "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount, scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Mask", "meaning": "how much of the inverted value is mixed into the original; default 1 uses only the new value"}, {"name": "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha", "meaning": "choose which channels the effect applies to"}, {"name": "Invert By", "meaning": "Complement sets x to 1 - x (default); Negate sets x to -x; Reciprocal sets x to 1 / x"}]

- Caveats: ["Complement works as expected only for values in the 0 to 1 range; other values give negative or out-of-range results, so a Clamp COP may be needed afterward."]

